  "identity_evidence": "The source labels Horton Lake west of Dorton Bridge, east of the coast and south of Lake Murray. The broad basin has a northwest water connection, a north shore descending eastward, an inset southwestern shore bend, an eastern hook and a southern stream. Original Horton Lake CBRLZ and its WALK20 exterior reproduce that sequence. Both inlet/outlet streams and the dashed road northwest of the lake are excluded from the polygon. Fine shoreline detail differs; this is a basin-position check.",
